libarchive's reader for RAR 1.5 to 4.x archives (archive_read_support_format_rar.c), as
XFiles patches it. update.sh applies this after copying the sources:
patch -p1 -d third_party/libarchive.

- Solid archives (MHD_SOLID). A member flagged FHD_SOLID keeps the decoder state of the
  compressed member before it: the window, now 4 MB and kept, its positions offset by
  lzss.base, the Huffman tables, the PPMd model and escape character, the repeat-match state
  and the filter programs. Stored members are not part of that stream. An empty member is
  either nothing to decode (new tables pending) or an LZ end-of-data marker that is decoded.
  A member's end-of-data marker is read even past its last byte (read_member_end()), since
  the next member continues after it.
- Option solid_skip=decode: skipping a member of a solid archive decodes it, so the members
  after it stay readable. Without it skipping is as fast as before, and a member that
  continues skipped ones fails to read with an error instead of decoding wrong.
- Filters in PPMd blocks (escape code 3), which failed with "Parsing filters is
  unsupported": expand_ppmd() is expand() for PPMd blocks, and filter blocks are decoded
  across PPMd and LZ blocks (expand_any()).
- PPMd blocks without a new escape character keep the last one instead of resetting it to 2,
  and the PPMd model's memory size no longer resizes and clears the window.
- A member ends once everything decoded before its end-of-data marker has gone out, so a
  PPMd member that ended with a match across the output buffer's end no longer loses bytes.
- RAR 2.0 compression (unp_ver 20 and 26), which was decoded as RAR 2.9 and failed: LZ and
  audio blocks, solid or not (parse_codes20(), expand20(), decode_audio20()). The block
  format, the meaning of the symbols and the audio predictor are ported from rardecode
  (https://github.com/nwaples/rardecode, BSD 2-clause; its notice is in the code). A RAR 2.0
  member ends at its size, and in a solid archive its data may hold more for the next member
  (read_member_end20()): an empty first member holds the tables, and an empty member before
  one that needs other codes holds the end of the block and a new header. This was worked
  out from archives that RAR 2.80 made.
- RAR 1.5 compression (unp_ver 15) fails with "RAR 1.5 compression is not supported".
- The blocks of RAR 1.5 to 2.x archives: the archive comment inside the main header and a
  file comment inside its file header are left out of their header's CRC (RAR 2.80's
  technote.txt). A recovery record's CRC covers its header and a Unix owner subblock's its
  data too, so either is accepted; authenticity blocks aren't checked. An archive may end
  after any block, without an end-of-archive block.
- read_next_symbol(): a short code near the end of the data, with fewer bits after it than a
  table lookup takes, is looked up with zeros after it instead of failing.

Archives that read before decode as before; RarReadingTest, SolidRar4Test, Rar2Test and
ArchiveFormatsTest cover them. Nothing here comes from UnRAR's source.

